# Campaign 2 closure — correctness, sustained performance, utility

**Global state: CORRECTNESS_BLOCKED.** A 120B runtime with plausible functional responses and sustained throughput is demonstrated on the physical target, and a new frozen task pilot observed a practical advantage. Independent numerical coverage for the production GPU8/32-slot path remains too narrow to certify robust exact routed execution. The campaign's >=4 tok/s sustained and short-latency goals were not met. This is an evidence boundary, not a physical impossibility result. Broad novelty remains **BROAD_NOVELTY_NO_GO / ENGINEERING_AND_MEASUREMENT_GO**.

Objective/base: C2 started 2026-09-26 13:49:33 UTC from clean lab commit `c67529e` on local branch `campaign/c2-correctness-usability-20260926-1349utc`. Physical host was reconfirmed: Ryzen AI 9 HX370, RTX4060 Laptop 8188 MiB with driver 615.71.09, 30 GiB reported RAM, target GGUF on internal `/dev/nvme0n1p3` Btrfs `/home`, not an external/remote filesystem. Target `ggml-org/gpt-oss-120b-GGUF` MXFP4 revision `238abdd290bb874b90a5da1b4549881b7d05c091`, 63,387,346,208 B, SHA-256 `582bd40f6886200101f4c4ed9f25f3fe80cc14c86e9e2b37746cd8904a0c622d`. Stock 20B SHA-256 `52f57ab7d3df3ba9173827c1c6832e73375553a846f3e32b49f1ae2daad688d4`. Stock backend `ggml-org/llama.cpp` SHA `4b1a27fa0eb875bbca4f6cfe936e3d65adc685c0`; streamed backend `freedomljc/llama.cpp` SHA `1248fd8fa8cfebaece5ea992e4d951c1e18bb9d5`. Binary and loaded-library SHA-256 values are in frozen protocols/run manifests. No backend source patch, quantization, routing, tokenizer, attention or sampler change was promoted.

