Performance/resource detail: C2-C was GPU8 (eight layers), 32 per-layer expert slots, context4096, batch256, microbatch32, eight CPU threads, four I/O threads, greedy/seed42/medium, no preload/repack, O_DIRECT expert reads, no prompt cache, one sequence/context. Enforced cgroup memory.max **18 GiB**, memory.swap.max=0; watchdog RSS17 GiB, GPU total<=7000 MiB, host MemAvailable>=6 GiB and CPU/GPU/NVMe limits 95/80/70 C. Peak C2-C `memory.peak` 15,344,664,576 B, GPU 3856 MiB, max CPU/GPU/NVMe 86/58/60.85 C; zero swap/max/OOM/kill events. On the 50-minute C2-E target run: peak cgroup 15,911,616,512 B, GPU 3858 MiB, max 90.375/58/60.85 C, zero swap/max/OOM/kill events; 8423 completion tokens in 2408.562 s decode = 3.497 tok/s on this different task mix. Device-exclusive physical NVMe bytes, per-tier host/device hits and H2D traffic are **DESCONHECIDO**. C2-C sampled process `read_bytes` rose 3.090 TB, C2-E target 4.442 TB; those counters are not physical device attribution. CPU/power-limit throttling behavior beyond sampled sensors is **DESCONHECIDO**.

The C1 24-slot sustained 2.733 tok/s and three short 24/32 A/B pairs (2.568→3.269 mean) are retained as historical comparisons with different coverage. No fresh same-protocol sustained24 control was run, so the 3.327 C2-C figure is not a causal sustained 24→32 speedup. No candidate `-ngl12`, larger microbatch, predictor, prefetch, speculative decoder or three-tier cache was promoted: C2-B's independent numerical gate was not cleared. New optimization intervention count **0/6**. C2-D's prefill timings locate the observable delay but do not identify an exclusive per-layer I/O or compute bottleneck. Token interval p50/p95 is **NOT_MEASURED**; SSE first-chunk arrival is not a per-token interval. The task runner's nonstream API did not expose TTFT or reasoning/final token split; total completion tokens and reasoning/final character counts are retained.

Utility decision: the new suite was fixed before model answers, with four development cases, twelve evaluation cases and correct/mutant validator checks. All twelve evaluation cases were run once per model; none was selected after seeing answers. The two target-only wins are real under the frozen 2048-token cap and validators. The ten shared successes, 11.478× time cost, short first-final latency of 74.506 s and narrow synthetic scope support a **selective fallback candidate** when the fast 20B produces no final answer at its cap, not default 120B use. A longer stock cap could alter those wins; it would be another prospectively frozen quality/cost experiment. No statistical significance or parameter-count causal claim follows from twelve cases. The earlier C1 8/10 tie remains unchanged.

Retained failures/limits: target smoke02 fails its 2.162 s telemetry boundary; 120B plain reference runs `c2-ref120b-cpu-all01/02` stopped at their declared secondary RSS guards without OOM and do not yield full-model parity; a first descriptive sustained report had an event-key bug, preserved under its original name with corrected `analysis-v2` authoritative. GPU8 plain full-reference weights alone exceed the RTX4060 VRAM budget, so no matching full-model GPU reference was run. Source audit and 20B fault injection do not replace an executed 120B in-flight eviction/stale publication or upload-error test. C2-E answers are functional tests, not proof of exact numeric computation across the token prefixes they traversed. Complete 4096-token prompt use, 8192 context, prefix reuse, physical-device-exclusive I/O and per-tier cache accounting remain NOT_RUN/DESCONHECIDO as documented.

Local evidence authority: `../LAB_STATE.md`, `../DECISIONS.md`, `../results/INDEX.md`, phase reports `C2-A` through `C2-F`, and `../results/c2-final-summary.json`. Raw stdout/stderr, one-second samples, answer texts and logit rows remain local and no-replace; compact gates, grades, comparison and source-hash publications are versioned. Old `../results/campaign-summary.json` is byte-preserved as an early C1 snapshot. No model process, watcher or localhost listener remained at closure. The C2 branch has local commits only; **no push, PR, merge or remote publication** occurred under this campaign's explicit instruction.

Next discriminating gate: qualify longer target token prefixes on a reference independent of the tested expert cache while preserving GPU8 placement or explicitly documenting a differential layer/kernel scope under the unchanged 18 GiB/zero-swap envelope. A new reference design must account for file-backed reclaim and avoid the RSS guard conflict that stopped both C2 attempts. Only after numerical coverage is sufficient should one profile the prefill wait/compute path and prospectively test a single placement or microbatch change against the 32-slot baseline. The selective fallback policy also needs a separate prospective latency/quality run if deployment is considered. These are reasons for a future experiment, not claims that this campaign completed them.
